@* The "Unsaved changes" popover of a settings form: non-modal, in the top
   layer along the bottom of the screen, shown by portal-settings.js while
   the form differs from what is stored. Discard puts the form back; Save
   posts it. Without the script the form posts like any other, so the
   popover simply stays hidden. *@
<div class="settings-unsaved" popover="manual" data-settings-unsaved>
    <span class="settings-unsaved__text">@L["Unsaved changes"]</span>
    <div class="settings-unsaved__actions">
        <button type="button" class="btn btn-danger-subtle" data-settings-discard>@L["Discard"]</button>
        <button type="submit" class="btn settings-unsaved__save">@L["Save"]</button>
    </div>
</div>
